y my 7 bomb now, it\'s a medium-strength bomb. If the landlord has a higher bomb (like a 2 or A), they can beat it. But if they don\'t, then my teammate can play next. \n\nAlternatively, if I pass, the landlord might play something else. But the current last play is the triplet with a 4. If I pass, the landlord could choose to play a card that my teammate can\'t easily beat, which might be risky. \n\nSince I have a bomb, which is a strong move, and the current play is a triplet with a single, using the bomb here is a good option. It allows me to take control of the turn and force the landlord to respond. If they have a higher bomb, they\'ll use it, but if not, my teammate can play next. \n\nSo the best move is to play the bomb with four 7s. That\'s the only valid move available besides passing, and passing might let the landlord take the lead. Therefore, playing the bomb is the better choice here.\n</think>\n\nEvaluation: The current last play is a triplet of 8s with a 4. I have a bomb (four 7s) available. As a peasant, playing the bomb now can assert control, force the landlord to respond, and potentially deplete their high-value bombs. Passing risks letting the landlord dictate the game flow.\n\nReason: Playing the bomb (four 7s) is optimal. It beats the current play, maintains initiative, and limits the landlord\'s opportunities to use stronger bombs later. Since the landlord holds 16 cards (including potential 2/A bombs), saving this bomb now maximizes strategic pressure while preserving resources for critical moments.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠7", "♥7", "♣7", "♦7"]}'}
